{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Your land, etc.</b> The metaphor above: a parable that their entire land was taken, and part of it is desolation with no person there, and part of it is burned with fire, and part of it — strangers consume its produce:" "<b>[consume it].</b> Like the sense of בעצבון תאכלנה (Genesis 3:17)." "And the sense of <b>like the overthrow of strangers.</b> He explains: your land is desolation. And it is possible that זרים is from the root זרם (Isaiah 32:2), and the mem would be a root letter and not a plural, and there would be two possible patterns."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:23.694689202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}